{"book":10,"chapter":17,"rubric":"LEARNING RUST / DATA AND ABSTRACTIONS / CHAPTER 17","slides":[{"title":"Product and sum","sub":"Chapter 17 · struct, enum, match","short":"Introduction","main":"struct is both; enum is one of; match takes apart and checks completeness.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["struct: both at once","enum: one of","match: take apart"],"captions":["A struct combines fields at once: both x and y, a product type","An enum chooses exactly one variant: circle, or rectangle, or point, a sum type","match takes a value apart by variant and checks that all are covered"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":180.0,"h":70.0,"text":"","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":130.0,"y":70.0,"w":56.0,"h":36.0,"text":"x\ni32","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"y","x":230.0,"y":70.0,"w":56.0,"h":36.0,"text":"y\ni32","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"x AND y","tone":"blue","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Circle(r)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Rect(w, h)","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":280.0,"y":60.0,"w":96.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Point","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"Circle OR Rect OR Point","tone":"yellow","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":40.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["match shape {","    Circle(r) => 3.14 * r * r,","    Rect(w, h) => w * h,","    Point => 0.0,","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":280.0}]],"cues":[14.6,26.4]}]},{"title":"Struct and memory","sub":"Fields, alignment","short":"struct","main":"Fields sit in a row on the stack; Rust reorders them, repr(C) does not.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Literal","Fields in a row","Alignment"],"captions":["A struct is created with a literal, fields are read with a dot; if a variable has the field's name, you do not repeat it","Fields sit in a row on the stack: two i32 make eight bytes, with no object header as in Python","The CPU likes aligned addresses: repr(C) leaves gaps between fields, while Rust reorders the fields and saves the space"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct Point { x: i32, y: i32 }","let p = Point { x: 1, y: 2 };","println!(\"{}\", p.x);"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m0","x":130.0,"y":70.0,"w":98.0,"h":26.0,"text":"x = 1","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"m1","x":230.0,"y":70.0,"w":98.0,"h":26.0,"text":"y = 2","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":104.0,"text":"size_of::<Point>() = 8","size":10.0,"mono":true},{"t":"text","id":"a","x":130.0,"y":46.0,"text":"+0","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":46.0,"text":"+4","size":8.5}],[{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":180.0,"y":20.0,"text":"#[repr(C)] { a: u8, b: u32, c: u8 }  = 12 bytes","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"c0","x":36.0,"y":44.0,"w":22.0,"h":26.0,"text":"a","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c1","x":84.0,"y":44.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"gap","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c2","x":168.0,"y":44.0,"w":94.0,"h":26.0,"text":"b","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c3","x":228.0,"y":44.0,"w":22.0,"h":26.0,"text":"c","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c4","x":276.0,"y":44.0,"w":70.0,"h":26.0,"text":"gap","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"text":"by default Rust reorders: b, a, c  = 8 bytes","size":8.5,"mono":true},{"t":"cell","id":"r0","x":108.0,"y":124.0,"w":94.0,"h":26.0,"text":"b","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r1","x":168.0,"y":124.0,"w":22.0,"h":26.0,"text":"a","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r2","x":192.0,"y":124.0,"w":22.0,"h":26.0,"text":"c","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r3","x":228.0,"y":124.0,"w":46.0,"h":26.0,"text":"gap","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[11.9,30.4]}]},{"title":"impl and derive","sub":"Methods and ready-made impls","short":"impl","main":"Methods go in impl; derive gives Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Default.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["impl","Associated function","derive"],"captions":["Methods are written in an impl block; self takes one of three forms: read, modify, or take","A function without self is called via the type name: Rect::new is just a conventional name, the language has no constructors","The derive attribute plugs in ready-made impls: debug output, cloning, comparison, default value"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Rect {","    fn area(&self) -> u32 {","        self.w * self.h","    }","}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["impl Rect {","    fn new(w: u32, h: u32) -> Rect {","        Rect { w, h }","    }","}","let r = Rect::new(3, 4);"],"hl":[5],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":140.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Debug","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":72.0,"w":140.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Clone","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":90.0,"y":104.0,"w":140.0,"h":24.0,"text":"PartialEq","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"f","x":90.0,"y":136.0,"w":140.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Default","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":270.0,"y":72.0,"w":160.0,"h":60.0,"text":"{:?}\nRect { w: 3, h: 4 }","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.9,26.2]}]},{"title":"Enums","sub":"Variants with data","short":"enum","main":"A value is exactly one variant with its own data.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Variants with data","Exactly one","In Python"],"captions":["Each variant carries its own data, and different data: a circle has a radius, a rectangle two sides, a point nothing","A value is in exactly one variant at any moment; reading a rectangle's radius is impossible by construction","In Python that is several classes and isinstance; here it is one type, and the compiler knows all the variants"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["enum Shape {","    Circle(f64),","    Rect(f64, f64),","    Point,","}"],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":19.0,"w":240.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Circle(2.0)","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Rect(w, h)","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.35},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Point","tone":"muted","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5,"o":0.35},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":120.0,"text":"let s = Shape::Circle(2.0);","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["class Circle: ...","class Rect: ...","if isinstance(s, Circle): ..."],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":16.0,"w":190.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":285.0,"y":56.0,"w":130.0,"h":34.0,"text":"enum Shape\none type","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":285.0,"y":100.0,"text":"all variants known","tone":"green","size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.1,24.3]}]},{"title":"Size of an enum","sub":"Tag and niche","short":"Size","main":"Size = tag + largest variant; Option<Box<T>> has no tag.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Tag + data","Sizes","Niche"],"captions":["The tagged union from the architecture chapters: a variant tag and a shared space for the payload","Size is the tag plus the largest variant, with alignment: an enum with no data takes one byte","An Option of a pointer needs no tag: address zero is never real, so it is given to None"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"t","x":60.0,"y":60.0,"w":60.0,"h":30.0,"text":"tag","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":190.0,"y":60.0,"w":180.0,"h":30.0,"text":"shared payload: 16 bytes","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"c","x":60.0,"y":100.0,"text":"Circle: 0","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"r","x":190.0,"y":100.0,"text":"Rect(w, h): tag 1 + two f64","size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"Shape = 8 + 16 = 24 bytes","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true}],[{"t":"bar","id":"b0","x":60.0,"y":120.0,"w":34.0,"hh":4.166666666666666,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"1"},{"t":"text","id":"l0","x":60.0,"y":142.0,"text":"enum{A,B,C}","size":7.5,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b1","x":140.0,"y":120.0,"w":34.0,"hh":8.333333333333332,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"2"},{"t":"text","id":"l1","x":140.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Option<u8>","size":7.5,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b2","x":220.0,"y":120.0,"w":34.0,"hh":33.33333333333333,"max":100.0,"tone":"blue","text":"8"},{"t":"text","id":"l2","x":220.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Option<u32>","size":7.5,"mono":true},{"t":"bar","id":"b3","x":300.0,"y":120.0,"w":34.0,"hh":100.0,"max":100.0,"tone":"yellow","text":"24"},{"t":"text","id":"l3","x":300.0,"y":142.0,"text":"Shape","size":7.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"cell","id":"p","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"Some(ptr)\n0x5a10…","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n~cell","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"None\n0x0000…","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"t~text","x":180.0,"y":110.0,"text":"Option<Box<T>> = 8 bytes, like Box<T>","tone":"green","size":10.0,"mono":true}]],"cues":[14.3,22.6]}]},{"title":"match","sub":"Exhaustive matching","short":"match","main":"All variants must be covered; under the hood, a jump table.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Arms","Exhaustive","Jump table"],"captions":["The first arm that fits runs; match is an expression with a value; the underscore catches the rest","Forget a variant and it will not build: add a variant to the enum and you see every place to update","Under the hood usually a jump table by tag, like a switch in assembly, but without falling through to the next arm"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let area = match shape {","    Circle(r) => 3.14 * r * r,","    Rect(w, h) => w * h,","    _ => 0.0,","};"],"hl":[1],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["match shape {","    Circle(r) => …,","    Rect(w, h) => …,","}"],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":240.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":330.0,"h":34.0,"text":"error[E0004]: non-exhaustive patterns:\n`Shape::Point` not covered","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"tag","x":60.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":30.0,"text":"tag = 1","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":190.0,"y":36.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"0 → Circle","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"1 → Rect","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":190.0,"y":104.0,"w":90.0,"h":22.0,"text":"2 → Point","tone":"muted","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":96.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":144.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"arm","x":300.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"w * h","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":236.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":250.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[13.0,26.6]}]},{"title":"Patterns","sub":"Tuples, ranges, guards","short":"Patterns","main":"Patterns nest; the if guard and the @ binding refine an arm.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Tuples and structs","Ranges and |","Guard and @"],"captions":["A pattern takes a tuple or struct apart right in the arm header; the rest is skipped with two dots","Ranges set boundaries, the vertical bar combines variants","After a pattern you can add an if condition, a guard; a name with @ binds the value after checking it against a pattern"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["match (x, y) {","    (0, 0) => \"center\",","    (a, 0) => \"on the x axis\",","    Point { x, .. } => …,","}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["match n {","    1..=9 => \"digit\",","    10 | 20 | 30 => \"round\",","    _ => \"other\",","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":36.0,"lines":["match n {","    x if x < 0 => \"negative\",","    d @ 1..=9 => …,","    _ => …,","}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[15.9,27.9]}]},{"title":"Option","sub":"Instead of null","short":"Option","main":"No value is None, not null: the type demands a check.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["No value: null","Methods","unwrap panics"],"captions":["If a value may be missing, its type is Option<T>: either Some with data, or None; an i32 is never \"empty\"","map, and_then, unwrap_or turn a chain of checks into a pipeline; the ? sign returns None from the function at once","unwrap pulls the value out but panics on None: keep it for tests and impossible cases"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":110.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Option<i32>","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"s","x":250.0,"y":40.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Some(5)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n","x":250.0,"y":74.0,"w":90.0,"h":24.0,"text":"None","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"i","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"i32 is always a number","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":142.0,"y1":56.0,"x2":202.0,"y2":44.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":142.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":202.0,"y2":74.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":50.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Some(3)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":150.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":".map(×2)","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":70.0,"h":28.0,"text":"Some(6)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":82.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":116.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":184.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":216.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"code","id":"c1","x":20.0,"y":120.0,"lines":["opt.map(|x| x * 2).unwrap_or(0)"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":180.0,"y":66.0,"w":320.0,"h":44.0,"text":"thread 'main' panicked at src/main.rs:3:\ncalled `Option::unwrap()` on a `None` value","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.9,26.9]}]},{"title":"if let and friends","sub":"Short forms of match","short":"if let","main":"if let, let else, while let and matches! are shorthand for match.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["if let","let else","while let","matches!"],"captions":["if let checks one pattern and binds names; the other variants are silently skipped","let else binds the value or leaves at once, so the main code stays flat","while let loops while the pattern matches: this is how you empty a stack","matches! answers with a single bool whether a value fits a pattern"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["if let Some(x) = opt {","    println!(\"{x}\");","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let Some(x) = opt else {","    return;","};","// from here on, x is a number"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["while let Some(top) = stack.pop() {","    println!(\"{top}\");","}"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.5,"lh":18.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["let ok = matches!(cmd, Cmd::Go | Cmd::Run);"],"hl":[0],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":18.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[10.2,22.4,28.2]}]},{"title":"match and ownership","sub":"Move or borrow","short":"Ownership","main":"match by value moves data, by reference it borrows.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Move","By reference","Mutable"],"captions":["match by value moves data into the bindings: the value is unavailable afterwards, the same move rules","If you still need the data, match a reference: match &opt makes the bindings references, and the value stays in place","With a mutable reference you change the data inside a variant in place: if let Some(x) = &mut o { *x += 1 }"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":30.0,"lines":["let o = Some(String::from(\"hi\"));","match o {","    Some(s) => println!(\"{s}\"),","    None => {}","}","println!(\"{:?}\", o);"],"hl":[2],"bad":[5],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0},{"t":"cell","id":"m","x":290.0,"y":140.0,"w":120.0,"h":22.0,"text":"borrow of moved value","tone":"red","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["let o = Some(String::from(\"hi\"));","match &o {","    Some(s) => println!(\"{s}\"),","    None => {}","}","println!(\"{:?}\", o);  // ok"],"hl":[1,2,5],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":14.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["let mut o = Some(5);","if let Some(x) = &mut o {","    *x += 1;","}","// o == Some(6)"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"rust","size":10.0,"lh":17.0,"w":300.0}]],"cues":[13.4,28.0]}]},{"title":"State machine","sub":"Impossible is unrepresentable","short":"States","main":"States are enum variants; a transition takes self by value.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["States","Transitions","Impossible"],"captions":["A door is an enum: open, closed, locked with a code; data exists only where it is needed","A method takes self by value and returns the new state: the old one ceases to exist","Instead of is_open and is_locked flags that can contradict each other, one type with no invalid combinations"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Open","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Closed","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Locked\n{ code }","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Open","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":34.0,"text":"Closed","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"l","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"Locked\n{ code }","tone":"yellow","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":226.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":238.0,"y2":62.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"a","x":125.0,"y":40.0,"text":"close","size":8.0},{"t":"text","id":"b","x":232.0,"y":40.0,"text":"lock","size":8.0},{"t":"text","id":"t","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"text":"fn next(self, a: Action) -> Door","size":9.5,"mono":true}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":8.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["is_open: bool","is_locked: bool","// open && locked ???"],"hl":[2],"bad":[2],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":17.0,"w":170.0},{"t":"cell","id":"e","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":150.0,"h":50.0,"text":"enum Door\n3 valid\nstates","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.6,30.6]}]},{"title":"Order, newtype, Default","sub":"Useful derives","short":"derive","main":"Field order is comparison order; a newtype is free; Default is built from the fields.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Field order","Newtype","Default"],"captions":["derive(Ord) compares fields lexicographically, in definition order: swap the fields and the sort order changes","A wrapper around a number is the same number at machine level, but a user cannot be confused with an order","derive(Default) builds a default value from the fields' defaults: 0, false, empty string, None"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":12.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["struct Version {","    major: u32,","    minor: u32,","    patch: u32,","}"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":150.0},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":280.0,"y":50.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1.2.9 < 1.10.0","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":280.0,"y":82.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2.0.0 > 1.99.9","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":280.0,"y":116.0,"text":"major first","size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"u","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":"UserId\n42","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":90.0,"y":112.0,"w":80.0,"h":40.0,"text":"OrderId\n42","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"x","x":250.0,"y":84.0,"w":130.0,"h":56.0,"text":"4 bytes each\ncannot be\ncompared ✕","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":40.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"u32 → 0","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"bool → false","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"String → \"\"","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":90.0,"y":130.0,"w":120.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Option<T> → None","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"code","id":"e","x":220.0,"y":60.0,"lines":["Config {","    retries: 3,","    ..Default::default()","}"],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":15.0,"w":150.0}]],"cues":[17.2,23.6]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"What's next","short":"Summary","main":"struct, enum, match are the basis of modeling; next, collections and Result.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Three tools","Rules","What's next"],"captions":["A struct collects fields, an enum chooses a variant, match takes apart and demands you cover everything","Enum size is tag plus largest variant; Option of a pointer is free; match by value moves, by reference borrows","Next, collections and errors: Vec, String, HashMap and the Result type, on which error handling rests"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"struct\nAND","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"enum\nOR","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":60.0,"w":100.0,"h":40.0,"text":"match\ntake apart","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"r1","x":180.0,"y":36.0,"w":320.0,"h":24.0,"text":"enum size = tag + largest variant","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r2","x":180.0,"y":68.0,"w":320.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Option<Box<T>> = 8 bytes, niche in zero","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r3","x":180.0,"y":100.0,"w":320.0,"h":24.0,"text":"match by value moves; by reference borrows","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"r4","x":180.0,"y":132.0,"w":320.0,"h":24.0,"text":"invalid states cannot be built","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":80.0,"y":66.0,"w":100.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Vec · String\nHashMap","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":220.0,"y":66.0,"w":110.0,"h":36.0,"text":"Result<T, E>\nand the ? operator","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e","x1":134.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":160.0,"y2":66.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.1,25.4]}]}]}